# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the server first (npm start), then click Send Request above any request.

### Every game: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games

### Games for a group of four (1, 2, 4 and 6): 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games?players=4

### Games of 30 minutes or less (2, 3, 5 and 6): 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games?maxMinutes=30

### Both filters at once (2 and 6): 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games?players=4&maxMinutes=30

### No game is made for a group of twelve, so an empty list: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games?players=12

### One game by its id: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games/4

### A game that isn't on the shelf: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/games/99

### Not a number at all: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/games/chess

### Add a game (it gets id 9): 201
POST http://localhost:3100/games
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Lantern Festival", "minPlayers": 2, "maxPlayers": 4, "minutes": 35 }

### The new game is on the shelf, until the server restarts: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/games/9

### An address the café's API doesn't know: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/snacks
